          "reasoning": "Baltimore gets the clearer starting-pitching edge. Brandon Young is at least stretched out as a traditional starter, typically working 4-6 innings on normal rest. Richard Lovelady's recent usage strongly suggests an opener/bulk arrangement rather than a real starter; on 2 days rest and with recent outings of 0.1, 1.0, 2.0, 0.2, and 0.2 innings, Washington is likely piecing together the first half of the game. That raises volatility and makes Baltimore more attractive in F3/F5. Counter-case: Young's underlying quality is still uncertain and if his command backs up early, Baltimore's edge shrinks fast."
