          "reasoning": "Bello has the better recent form ceiling, with two strong starts in his last two, but his last five still show meaningful volatility and earlier blow-up risk. Holmes has been shorter and less efficient, with recurring walk issues and limited likelihood of working deep. For first-5 specifically, Bello narrows the gap more than the full-game line suggests, but ATL still holds a slight edge because Holmes is facing a below-average BOS lineup while Bello faces the deeper, more dangerous lineup. Main counter-case: if Bello's sinker/change command from his last two turns is real, BOS can win the starter matchup outright."
