          "role": "contrarian",
          "game_winner": "DET",
          "reasoning": "The obvious narrative is 'struggling Flaherty vs reliable Gausman,' but this ignores Gausman's recent 4.2 IP, 6-ER meltdown and Flaherty's ability to generate swings and misses (10 Ks in last good start). DET's offense is due for positive regression on balls in play (.240 team AVG is 30 points below xBA). The sharpest value lies in fading the public's assumption that Flaherty cannot survive the lineup twice. COUNTER-CASE: Flaherty's command issues are mechanical and persistent; betting on a bounce-back against a disciplined TOR lineup that doesn't chase is catching a falling knife."
